  "plain": "A man named Charles, from a company called Exodus Propulsion, says that in the 2020s they put their thrusters on a scale, switched them on, and saw them get lighter, and that flipping them over made them heavier. He says the work is now going through peer review, meaning outside experts are checking it, and that it is part of their second patent application, the paperwork for legally protecting an invention. If true, it would be a device that pushes against gravity without burning fuel."
